repo:objectstack#4 · os-justin · session_01QSeKYpEsWWE9Y5YtSsDgqZ

## 席位核对 — ACCEPT · L1 · head `5568fa63a1698f656c29f4e2145301125d732d28` · 2026-11-25T05:57Z

- **Scope.** +241/−0 in 3 new files: `ui/packages/app-shell/src/views/studio-design/studioMenuPlacement.ts`, its `.test.ts`, and `.changeset/37200-studio-menu-placement.md`. The PR is a draft, `mergeable_state` is clean, the body says `Fixes #37200`, and both declaration lines (`Clause-②: no`, `Metadata-protocol: none`) are in the body and the changeset. Nothing imports the table, so there is no wiring, as the card requires.
- **Rows against the ruling (#37192, 7151834490 + 7151811337).** The 常用 rows are object · app, page, dashboard, report · flow · permission · agent, tool, skill. That is the ruled set in the ruled order, and these 10 rows come first (indices 0–9). The other 22 rows are 高级. picklist (adjustment 1) and email_template are among them. The AI types are 常用 and drawn last (adjustment 2). The OWD overview (默认共享) is not a type, so it has no row here; #37201 places it with the other non-type entries.
- **Rows against ADR-0084 on main (`docs/adr/0084-…md:161-195`, merged in #37219 `3b87ff7eb05`).** The ADR blob at head is byte-identical to `origin/main`. All 32 rows match the ADR's Tier column. Inside each group they follow the ADR's Order column: data: object, picklist, hook, mapping, object_extension, seed. ui: app, page, dashboard, report, view, action, dataset. automation: flow, job. system: doc, book, email_template, translation, api, datasource, external_catalog. security: permission, position, assignment_rule, sharing_rule, queue, capability. ai: agent, tool, skill, ai_context. ADR item 6 (`:310`) places `ai_context` at 高级, last in ai, and the table follows that direction.
- **Count, and why `field` is excluded.** `DEFAULT_METADATA_TYPE_REGISTRY` (`packages/spec/src/kernel/metadata-plugin.zod.ts`) has 33 entries at head. `HIDDEN_DIRECTORY_TYPES = new Set(['field', 'package'])` (`ui/packages/app-shell/src/views/metadata-admin/directoryScope.ts:15`, with the reason "`field` is edited inside its object") is applied first in `scopeDirectoryEntries` (`:36`). That function is the filter the menu's types pass through (`studioMenuModel.ts`, `buildStudioMenu`'s doc comment). `package` is not a registered type, so 33 − 1 = 32 listable types. The ADR's `field` row carries `—` in both Order and Tier (`:169`), and the ADR regex's `(\d+)` deliberately skips it. Excluding `field` is justified. The test imports the same `HIDDEN_DIRECTORY_TYPES` set, so a future change to it moves the pin too.
- **Pins go red. I re-ran them myself instead of trusting the report.** I ported the 12 assertions into a standalone `tsx` harness (`pr-37232/h/pins.mts`, results in `pr-37232/h/ablations.txt`). It runs on the head's `studioMenuPlacement.ts`, the head's ADR and the head's registry. Baseline: 12/12 green. Every mutation went red:
  - remove `hook`: 5 red;
  - swap app/page: 2 red (O1 and the ADR order pin for `group ui`);
  - swap view/action inside 高级: 2 red;
  - add `bogus`: 4 red;
  - add `field`: 5 red;
  - duplicate `hook`: 4 red;
  - newly registered `form`, with no row: 3 red;
  - `job` retiered to common: 4 red;
  - ADR `ai_context` Order 4→0: 1 red (`ai`);
  - ADR `picklist` set to 常用: 1 red;
  - ADR `seed` row dropped: 3 red.

  So the pins catch a missing row, a misordered row, a duplicate, an unknown or hidden row, and an unplaced new type. The registry pin reads the live registry, not a copy.
- **How robust the ADR parse is.** `ADR_ROW` is anchored on `| **Group** | \`domain\` | N | \`type\`… | 常用|高级 |` after `trim()`, so CRLF and trailing spaces still parse (both ablations green). It does require exactly one space around each pipe. It fails closed, though: a double space on one row makes the count pin go red (31 ≠ 32), and the tier pin names the type (`seed`). A table re-aligned by a formatter would drop the count to 0, which is red, never a silent pass. No formatter or prettier config touches `docs/adr`. No other table in the ADR matches the pattern, and the count pin would catch one that did. The relative path `../`×6 resolves to the repo root. That is acceptable, see N2.
- **Changeset.** The diff is not test-only: it adds an exported source module to `@object-ui/app-shell` (private, but versioned under `privatePackages.version: true`). So a changeset is owed, and one is present. It is `patch` with `Metadata-protocol: none` (a UI-only table that adds nothing authorable), which is the level AGENTS.md post-task step 3 gives for `none`. `Check Changeset` is green.
- **Check-runs at head.** 51 runs, every one `success` or `skipped`, none failing or pending. Green: Test UI (9 of the 16 shards planned, plus the aggregate), Type Check UI, Lint UI, Build & E2E UI, Live E2E UI, Check Changeset, PR-body guards, Governed Surface Queue Guard, Dogfood Regression Gate, Test Core (aggregate). The Core shards were skipped because nothing changed outside `ui/`.
- **K = 6.** Merge-base `8b74082f1ab4` against `origin/main` `a03c3d4e3c8`. The ADR, the registry and `directoryScope.ts` are unchanged between head and main, so the pins hold on main as it is now.
- **Overlap with #37201.** None. #37201 will edit `studioMenuModel.ts`, its test (`:64`), `StudioMenu.tsx` and `ui/packages/i18n/src/namespaces/studio/{en,zh}.ts`, plus whatever `always` list it re-points. This PR adds only new files. #37201 will import `STUDIO_MENU_PLACEMENT` and does not need to edit it. The open designer PRs #37168, #37169 and #37089 touch none of these three files.
- **Dev report (7153810065).** It matches the diff. The out-of-scope notes are accurate: ADR-0146 still says 32 types, and `studioAddressTable.test.ts` does not exist (the pattern lives in `studioAddress.test.ts`). Both are for the seat to route. They are not open items on this PR.

- N1 — The `## Pins` block of `studioMenuPlacement.ts`'s doc comment names only the registry pin. The literal-order pin and the ADR-0084 pin, which the changeset describes, are not mentioned. Also, "the menu applies that rule when it reads this list" (for a type with no row) is written in the present tense, but nothing reads the list yet. Both are fine to fold into #37201's edit.
- N2 — `ADR_ROW` hard-codes single spaces around pipes. It fails closed (see above), so this is cosmetic. ` *` around the pipes would make it tolerate a hand-padded row.
- N3 — How far CI reaches (out of card scope, a carrier candidate). The `ui:` paths filter in `ci.yml` (`:735-771`) does not list `docs/adr/**`. A PR that edits only ADR-0084's type table would not start Test UI, so the ADR pin would go red on the next unrelated `ui/` PR instead of on the PR that caused it. The pin is always-on through `select-affected-tests.mjs`, so it never goes stale silently. This is the same shape as the existing `app-shell/src/__tests__/product-neutral-renderer.ratchet.test.ts` reading ADR-0060, so it is precedent and not a defect introduced here.
- N4 — The PR body's ablation red counts for the row mutations (remove `hook` 3, swap app/page 1) are readings from before the ADR pin existed. At the final head the same mutations give 5 and 2 red, because the ADR pin fires as well. They are red either way, so the evidence still holds, but the head each count came from should be named.

No must-fix, no should-fix.
